    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0614" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/3047</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barclay</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1387</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi>
                </p>
                <p>His Britannic Majesty’s Chargé d’Affaires presents his compliments to the Acting
                    Secretary of State and has the honour to inform him, by direction of His
                    Majesty’s Principal Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs, that His Majesty’s
                    Government have received and considered the Memorandum from the State Department
                    (undated) which was received at this Embassy on the 19th November last, on the
                    subject of Liberia.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d408-f1"/> His Majesty’s Government
                    appreciate the force of the United States’ contention and suggest, therefore,
                    that the subject might be considered with other analogous questions at the
                    approaching Peace Conference. The United States Embassy in London, who have
                    enquired the views of His Majesty’s Government on the proposals, have been
                    informed similarly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-15">December 15,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d408-f1" n="2" xml:id="d408-f1-content">
                <p>For the substance of this memorandum (sent also to the French Embassy), see <ref
                        target="frus1918#pg_545">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1918, p. 545</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
